<h1>Set up gallery feed</h1>

<p>
    Visual Studio is capable of subscribing to extension feeds, so you will be notified
    of any updates to extensions found in this gallery. You will only be notified of any updates to extensions that you already have installed.
</p>

<section>
    <h2>Get the Open VSIX Gallery extension</h2>
    <p>
        To get automatic updates to installed extensions that publish nightly builds to this website,
        simply install the
        <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=MadsKristensen.VSIXGallery-nightlybuilds">
            Open VSIX Gallery
        </a>
        extension. It registers the main feed in Visual Studio for you. If you use Visual Studio Enterprise
        and want to choose specific feeds instead, continue with the manual setup below.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Choose the right feed</h2>
    <p>There are several feeds in this gallery you can subscribe to.</p>

    <dl>
        <dt>The main feed</dt>
        <dd>
            By subscribing to the <a href="/feed/">main feed</a> you will be notified by
            Visual Studio whenever any of the extensions in this gallery are updated. The feed
            contains all extensions available.
        </dd>

        <dt>Feed per author</dt>
        <dd>
            Each extension author has their own feed, so you can choose to subscribe to one or more
            authors' extensions.
        </dd>

        <dt>Feed for individual extension</dt>
        <dd>
            If you're only interested in updates to a specific extension, you can subscribe to its feed.
        </dd>
    </dl>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Set up a feed manually</h2>
    <p>
        Additional extension galleries are a Visual Studio Enterprise feature. In Visual Studio 2022,
        open <strong>Tools &gt; Options &gt; Environment &gt; Extensions</strong>. Under
        <strong>Additional Extension Galleries</strong>, select <strong>Add</strong>.
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>Enter a descriptive name, such as <strong>Open VSIX Gallery</strong>.</li>
        <li>Enter the feed URL. For the main feed, use <a href="/feed/">https://www.vsixgallery.com/feed/</a>.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>OK</strong> to save the gallery.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        See Microsoft&rsquo;s
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/visualstudio/ide/configure-extension-update-options#add-private-extension-galleries"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">extension gallery documentation</a>
        for the current Visual Studio instructions.
    </p>
</section>
